MustFlushRegion: answer the buffer cache part without its lock for never-GPU-written pages.
Port of zortos293/Eglantine 2b70fc5 (#413). The split's front asks MustFlushRegion before each macro
DMA read and waited on buffer_cache.mutex, which the back holds through each draw (upstream measured
8% of the OoT front waiting; not measured on this port). BufferCache::IsRegionGpuModified answers from
gpu_modified_ranges, and both places that add to it (MarkWrittenBuffer, DMACopy's mirrored ranges)
call memory_tracker.MarkRegionAsGpuModified -> GpuWrittenPages::Mark over a covering range BEFORE the
add; marks never clear. DMACopy used to mark after the add, which left a window where an unsynchronized
caller (GPU::InvalidateRegion with preserve_gpu_writes) saw no mark, skipped the lock and then let
the invalidation drop the just-added GPU range: it now marks first (Subtract/Add order unchanged).
So on Switch 2 (g_nx2_ampere) a range with no marked page (GpuWrittenPages::Any false, full bitmap
incl. image marks) has no buffer-GPU-modified range yet and skips the lock; once a page is marked the
lock is taken and waits for the add. Wraps and ranges past the 36-bit bitmap answer true and take it.
Non-Ampere, QueryCache and TextureCache checks are unchanged.
